1
00:00:14,615 --> 00:00:19,953
HELLO, TWENTY - WONHEE

2
00:00:20,287 --> 00:00:23,891
HELLO, TWENTY - WONHEE
EPISODE 4

3
00:00:23,957 --> 00:00:25,792
Hello.

4
00:00:27,594 --> 00:00:30,464
BOUNCING WITH EXCITEMENT TODAY

5
00:00:30,831 --> 00:00:32,499
GRAND ENTRANCE AS THE BACKDROP

6
00:00:32,566 --> 00:00:34,067
Awesome.

7
00:00:34,134 --> 00:00:36,169
Can you tell the viewers where we are?

8
00:00:36,236 --> 00:00:37,704
Everland.

9
00:00:38,405 --> 00:00:39,640
FROM THRILLING RIDES

10
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:42,709
TO PICTURESQUE SCENES
STRAIGHT FROM FAIRY TALES

11
00:00:43,243 --> 00:00:44,511
A LAND OF FUN AND THRILLS

12
00:00:44,945 --> 00:00:48,415
TODAY'S SHOOT TAKES PLACE IN EVERLAND,
THE LAND OF FANTASY

13
00:00:48,582 --> 00:00:51,518
Today, you'll enjoy everything
this theme park has to offer.

14
00:00:51,585 --> 00:00:54,121
I'M SO IN

15
00:00:54,187 --> 00:00:56,490
But you'll have to earn it through work.

16
00:00:56,557 --> 00:00:58,025
WORK

17
00:01:01,261 --> 00:01:02,496
I'M OUT

18
00:01:02,563 --> 00:01:03,730
Wonhee.

19
00:01:03,797 --> 00:01:05,032
DESPERATE

20
00:01:07,768 --> 00:01:10,571
But I want to ride the T-Express.

21
00:01:10,637 --> 00:01:15,475
Being an adult means
dealing with responsibilities.

22
00:01:15,542 --> 00:01:17,678
And they're too much to bear.

23
00:01:17,744 --> 00:01:19,246
You'll work as a part-timer

24
00:01:19,313 --> 00:01:21,081
- at a couple of rides here
- Okay.

25
00:01:21,148 --> 00:01:23,784
to experience the harsh reality.

26
00:01:23,850 --> 00:01:26,119
Wow, I'm already loving this.

27
00:01:26,486 --> 00:01:28,689
Do you want to call your partner
for the day?

28
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:31,391
Girlie.

29
00:01:33,827 --> 00:01:34,728
Eunchae.

30
00:01:35,128 --> 00:01:37,364
ADORBS

31
00:01:37,898 --> 00:01:39,633
- Eunchae.
- It's been so long.

32
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:42,135
EUNCHAE OF LE SSERAFIM
Welcome. How have you been?

33
00:01:42,202 --> 00:01:43,837
You must be busy promoting your new song.

34
00:01:43,904 --> 00:01:45,572
Yes, we're pretty busy.

35
00:01:45,639 --> 00:01:47,107
Still, I had to come

36
00:01:47,174 --> 00:01:50,510
because I've never been
on a variety show with you.

37
00:01:50,911 --> 00:01:53,013
- I've been looking forward to this.
- Me too.

38
00:01:53,647 --> 00:01:54,948
Do you enjoy rides?

39
00:01:55,015 --> 00:01:57,384
Not at all.

40
00:01:57,451 --> 00:01:58,285
Oh, no.

41
00:01:58,352 --> 00:02:01,555
THIS 21-YEAR-OLD IS FRIGHTENED OF THEM
I don't enjoy them.

42
00:02:01,622 --> 00:02:04,057
<i>The rain is mirroring my mood today.</i>

43
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:05,826
<i>You poor thing.</i>

44
00:02:05,892 --> 00:02:08,462
Please change into the uniforms
before your shift.

45
00:02:09,029 --> 00:02:10,530
So cute.

46
00:02:10,597 --> 00:02:12,366
It's all green.

47
00:02:12,432 --> 00:02:14,501
GROOVING

48
00:02:15,102 --> 00:02:19,206
LET'S GET OUR ENERGY UP
BEFORE OUR SHIFT BEGINS

49
00:02:19,272 --> 00:02:21,408
- Are you ready to get changed?
- Yes.

50
00:02:21,475 --> 00:02:22,876
Let's go.

51
00:02:22,943 --> 00:02:24,311
- Over there.
- Okay.

52
00:02:24,378 --> 00:02:26,279
- Let's do this.
- All right.

53
00:02:26,346 --> 00:02:27,814
- We've got this.
- Sure.

54
00:02:27,881 --> 00:02:29,716
Do you prefer your left side
or your right side?

55
00:02:29,783 --> 00:02:31,518
- My right.
- Nice, I prefer my left.

56
00:02:31,585 --> 00:02:32,419
EXCITED SQUEALING

57
00:02:33,286 --> 00:02:35,789
WILL THIS PAIR DO A GOOD JOB TODAY?

58
00:02:35,856 --> 00:02:37,190
<i>- Wow, look.</i>
<i>- This is it.</i>

59
00:02:37,257 --> 00:02:38,325
<i>It's my first time.</i>

60
00:02:38,392 --> 00:02:40,627
FIRST WORK SITE, T-EXPRESS
NOW CALLED MONIMO RUSH

61
00:02:41,728 --> 00:02:43,797
HERE COME THE GIRLIES

62
00:02:43,864 --> 00:02:45,098
- Hello.
- Hello.

63
00:02:45,165 --> 00:02:46,233
Welcome.

64
00:02:46,299 --> 00:02:47,668
Hello.

65
00:02:48,568 --> 00:02:49,836
JAZZ HANDS

66
00:02:49,903 --> 00:02:53,440
I'm Jang Hye-yeong,
a ride operator for T-Express.

67
00:02:53,507 --> 00:02:56,576
- It's nice to meet you.
- It's nice to meet you.

68
00:02:56,943 --> 00:02:59,780
We have a set of tasks to complete
before guests arrive.

69
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:03,383
- Let me give you a briefing.
- Okay.

70
00:03:03,784 --> 00:03:05,185
What do we have to do?

71
00:03:05,252 --> 00:03:06,720
First off,

72
00:03:06,787 --> 00:03:10,123
we'll check beneath the ride
for lost items

73
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:14,428
- and pick up any trash.
- Okay.

74
00:03:14,494 --> 00:03:19,499
Next, we'll check the lap bars
to ensure our guests' safety.

75
00:03:19,566 --> 00:03:22,069
- You will test their condition.
- Oh, really?

76
00:03:22,135 --> 00:03:23,870
Do we perhaps go on the ride, too?

77
00:03:24,504 --> 00:03:26,239
It's raining today, so...

78
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:29,876
GETTING HER HOPES UP
<i>I don't enjoy them.</i>

79
00:03:30,377 --> 00:03:33,213
PLEASE...
<i>But I want to ride the T-Express.</i>

80
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:36,049
But if it stops, you can.

81
00:03:36,116 --> 00:03:37,918
- Okay.
- Great.

82
00:03:37,984 --> 00:03:40,821
THEIR REACTIONS ARE POLAR OPPOSITES

83
00:03:41,288 --> 00:03:43,990
Congrats.

84
00:03:44,057 --> 00:03:46,393
- Shall we, then?
- Yes.

85
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:47,728
- Let's go.
- Okay.

86
00:03:47,794 --> 00:03:48,829
LET'S GET TO WORK

87
00:03:49,396 --> 00:03:51,832
STEP 1
CLEAN THE AREA UNDER THE RIDE

88
00:03:52,032 --> 00:03:53,700
When we cross the track,

89
00:03:53,767 --> 00:03:55,769
we have to stick to the yellow lines.

90
00:03:55,836 --> 00:03:56,837
Follow me.

91
00:03:57,804 --> 00:03:58,972
This way.

92
00:03:59,039 --> 00:04:00,674
It's slippery. Watch your step.

93
00:04:01,541 --> 00:04:03,210
When we enter the area under the tracks,

94
00:04:03,376 --> 00:04:05,011
we must wear a safety helmet.

95
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:07,247
- Please take one each.
- Okay.

96
00:04:07,314 --> 00:04:08,749
PUTTING THEM ON

97
00:04:08,815 --> 00:04:10,150
Make sure to fasten the strap.

98
00:04:10,217 --> 00:04:11,551
SAFETY HELMETS ON
Great.

99
00:04:11,618 --> 00:04:12,552
Now, let's go.

100
00:04:12,619 --> 00:04:14,254
- Okay.
- Great.

101
00:04:14,321 --> 00:04:15,355
Let's go.

102
00:04:15,422 --> 00:04:17,057
OFF TO THEIR FIRST TASK

103
00:04:17,657 --> 00:04:22,395
We're currently under the tracks
of the roller coaster.

104
00:04:22,462 --> 00:04:24,231
As you can see, there's trash here.

105
00:04:24,297 --> 00:04:25,999
We have to collect them.

106
00:04:26,066 --> 00:04:27,701
We often find guests' missing items

107
00:04:27,768 --> 00:04:31,204
such as cell phones,
lip products, and heat packs.

108
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:32,973
They should've left them on the platform.

109
00:04:33,039 --> 00:04:34,007
That's right.

110
00:04:34,074 --> 00:04:37,377
We always encourage them to leave
their belongings on the platform.

111
00:04:38,378 --> 00:04:40,313
It's cleaner than I thought.

112
00:04:40,380 --> 00:04:42,048
- I found a phone case.
- That looks like...

113
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:43,650
- It's for an older model.
- Right?

114
00:04:43,717 --> 00:04:46,019
It looks like the back cover
of an older model.

115
00:04:46,086 --> 00:04:48,221
I don't think
the owner will return to get it.

116
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:49,322
- Right.
- Yes.

117
00:04:49,389 --> 00:04:51,424
If the owner is likely
to come back to get it,

118
00:04:51,491 --> 00:04:52,993
- do we keep them elsewhere?
- Yes.

119
00:04:53,059 --> 00:04:54,861
We can hold on to them

120
00:04:54,928 --> 00:04:56,596
before handing them over
to lost-and-found.

121
00:04:56,663 --> 00:04:57,831
I found a hand mirror.

122
00:04:57,898 --> 00:05:00,333
- It's broken. Be careful.
- A mirror.

123
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:02,002
Oh, it's cracked.

124
00:05:02,068 --> 00:05:04,171
COLLECTED THE BROKEN MIRROR
Let's go.

125
00:05:04,404 --> 00:05:07,374
I thought there would be
more lost items here.

126
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:11,311
A section with more lost items
is actually up ahead.

127
00:05:11,378 --> 00:05:13,680
- Is it the prized section?
- Yes, the one at the start.

128
00:05:13,747 --> 00:05:15,949
- The steep dive early on.
- Oh, I see.

129
00:05:16,016 --> 00:05:18,285
That's where many people drop their items.

130
00:05:18,351 --> 00:05:20,854
- Be careful not to hit this beam.
- Okay.

131
00:05:22,088 --> 00:05:24,758
- Look, we've got a credit card.
- A credit card?

132
00:05:24,825 --> 00:05:27,627
- We should check the owner's name.
- Let's use that.

133
00:05:27,694 --> 00:05:29,896
- Whose card is it?
- Tell us.

134
00:05:29,963 --> 00:05:31,331
- "Cho Ha-yeon."
- Cho?

135
00:05:31,398 --> 00:05:33,366
- "Cho Ha-yeon."
- Ms. Cho Ha-yeon.

136
00:05:33,433 --> 00:05:36,236
- Why didn't you come back for it?
- You shouldn't have put it in the pocket.

137
00:05:36,303 --> 00:05:40,207
Could we perhaps use it
to get some snacks later?

138
00:05:40,273 --> 00:05:42,409
Hang on, I found a Pokémon card.

139
00:05:42,475 --> 00:05:44,611
- A Pokémon card?
- Which Pokémon is it?

140
00:05:44,678 --> 00:05:46,847
PLEASE LEAVE POKÉMON CARDS AT THE PLATFORM
"Duraludon."

141
00:05:47,247 --> 00:05:49,115
You fit right in.

142
00:05:49,182 --> 00:05:51,351
What does that even mean?

143
00:05:51,418 --> 00:05:53,386
- Just perfect.
- Thanks.

144
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:54,554
Good job.

145
00:05:56,156 --> 00:05:58,291
ENDLESS CLEANING

146
00:05:58,658 --> 00:06:00,160
WONHEE AND EUNCHAE HUSTLE

147
00:06:00,227 --> 00:06:02,195
- I found another Pokémon card.
- What?

148
00:06:02,262 --> 00:06:03,530
They must belong to the same person.

149
00:06:03,597 --> 00:06:05,131
I'll go to the other side to get it.

150
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:06,166
I guess we should.

151
00:06:06,233 --> 00:06:08,001
We can go through here.

152
00:06:08,068 --> 00:06:09,870
- Please watch your heads.
- Okay.

153
00:06:09,936 --> 00:06:10,770
Be careful.

154
00:06:10,837 --> 00:06:12,472
- Oh, dear.
- Please be careful.

155
00:06:13,573 --> 00:06:16,676
UP ABOVE, THE TRAIN WHIZZES BY

156
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:22,015
Wow, that looks so fun.

157
00:06:22,315 --> 00:06:24,951
Tell the world I'm not riding that.

158
00:06:25,151 --> 00:06:27,320
She won't be riding it.

159
00:06:27,587 --> 00:06:30,490
- Eunchae refuses to go on it.
- I just can't.

160
00:06:30,557 --> 00:06:33,693
FEARS ASIDE, THEY GET BACK TO CLEANING

161
00:06:34,628 --> 00:06:36,162
Is it coming this way?

162
00:06:36,229 --> 00:06:38,064
Does the train have just one drop?

163
00:06:38,131 --> 00:06:40,400
- There are 12 drops in total.
- What?

164
00:06:41,501 --> 00:06:43,169
A whopping 12 times?

165
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:46,640
We'll now go check the lap bars.

166
00:06:46,706 --> 00:06:49,109
You can go on the test ride to confirm...

167
00:06:49,175 --> 00:06:52,145
...to confirm its safety.

168
00:06:52,212 --> 00:06:53,046
- Okay.
- Okay.

169
00:06:53,613 --> 00:06:55,582
You'll ride it, right?

170
00:06:57,717 --> 00:06:59,286
PROTECT EUNCHAE
Eunchae, I'm sorry.

171
00:06:59,352 --> 00:07:01,521
- Sorry.
- Tell her, Wonhee.

172
00:07:01,721 --> 00:07:02,756
For the guests' safety--

173
00:07:02,822 --> 00:07:03,957
I'm down!

174
00:07:04,024 --> 00:07:06,026
WONHEE'S BETRAYAL

175
00:07:06,293 --> 00:07:08,662
Great. Let's move, then.

176
00:07:08,728 --> 00:07:09,796
- Okay.
- Let's go.

177
00:07:13,066 --> 00:07:15,402
<i>I get to work at Everland,</i>
<i>all thanks to you.</i>

178
00:07:15,468 --> 00:07:16,436
OFF TO CHECK THE LAP BARS

179
00:07:17,037 --> 00:07:20,073
SAFETY IS A MUST FOR THRILLING RIDES

180
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:23,143
ALL THE LAP BARS MUST BE CHECKED
ONE BY ONE

181
00:07:26,579 --> 00:07:29,683
STEP 2
CHECK THE LAP BARS

182
00:07:30,050 --> 00:07:33,086
In the morning, all the levers are raised.

183
00:07:33,153 --> 00:07:36,656
We'll lower the lap bars
just as we do when we have guests.

184
00:07:36,723 --> 00:07:37,590
Before that...

185
00:07:37,958 --> 00:07:39,659
- Clear.
- Once the order is given,

186
00:07:39,726 --> 00:07:42,362
- put your body weight to lower them.
- Our body weight?

187
00:07:42,429 --> 00:07:44,331
Otherwise, it'll put
too much strain on your arms.

188
00:07:44,397 --> 00:07:46,132
So make sure to use your body weight.

189
00:07:46,199 --> 00:07:47,567
- Try it yourselves.
- Okay.

190
00:07:49,903 --> 00:07:51,638
- I'm a dummy.
- You'll wear your arms that way.

191
00:07:51,705 --> 00:07:52,806
- Really?
- It's better

192
00:07:52,872 --> 00:07:54,207
to push down with your body weight.

193
00:07:54,674 --> 00:07:57,143
- So I should lean forward.
- Like this.

194
00:07:57,210 --> 00:07:59,112
- Like Michael Jackson, right?
- Yes.

195
00:07:59,179 --> 00:08:00,380
Like this.

196
00:08:00,447 --> 00:08:02,048
Yes, that's correct.

197
00:08:02,115 --> 00:08:03,583
- Great.
- You're hilarious.

198
00:08:03,650 --> 00:08:04,751
WONHEE JACKSON

199
00:08:04,818 --> 00:08:05,852
Like...

200
00:08:07,087 --> 00:08:08,588
That's perfect.

201
00:08:08,655 --> 00:08:10,256
It takes longer than I expected.

202
00:08:10,523 --> 00:08:12,826
- Actually, you have to go faster.
- Really?

203
00:08:12,892 --> 00:08:14,160
We fly through these.

204
00:08:14,227 --> 00:08:15,695
WE WILL ALSO MOVE FASTER

205
00:08:16,563 --> 00:08:17,664
Good job.

206
00:08:18,231 --> 00:08:19,366
LAST LAP BAR CHECKED

207
00:08:19,432 --> 00:08:23,370
I'll lower the bars on the other side.

208
00:08:23,837 --> 00:08:27,140
- Can we see how fast you go?
- Do you want a demonstration?

209
00:08:27,207 --> 00:08:29,175
- Of course!
- I can do this really fast.

210
00:08:29,242 --> 00:08:30,176
HIGH ANTICIPATION

211
00:08:31,644 --> 00:08:34,147
SPEED ON ANOTHER LEVEL

212
00:08:34,347 --> 00:08:36,349
- You're so quick.
- You'll need a hearty breakfast

213
00:08:36,416 --> 00:08:38,685
- before coming to work.
- Definitely.

214
00:08:38,752 --> 00:08:40,620
As newbies, we had no idea

215
00:08:40,687 --> 00:08:42,555
- and skipped breakfast.
- Right.

216
00:08:42,622 --> 00:08:44,290
CLEARED IN NO TIME

217
00:08:44,357 --> 00:08:48,361
We were saving room for the food here,
so we skipped breakfast.

218
00:08:48,828 --> 00:08:50,630
Our cafeteria has great food.

219
00:08:51,131 --> 00:08:53,566
I heard the staff cafeteria was amazing.

220
00:08:53,633 --> 00:08:54,667
That's true.

221
00:08:54,868 --> 00:08:57,170
Now, let's send the train on a test run.

222
00:08:57,404 --> 00:09:00,807
This button right here starts the train.

223
00:09:00,874 --> 00:09:03,576
We call this top button "Yellow."

224
00:09:03,643 --> 00:09:04,477
Over there on Post 1,

225
00:09:04,744 --> 00:09:07,380
there is a button
just like the one here at Post 6.

226
00:09:07,847 --> 00:09:10,116
<i>When all ride operators</i>
<i>stand behind the yellow line</i>

227
00:09:10,183 --> 00:09:12,218
<i>after confirming the guests' safety,</i>

228
00:09:12,285 --> 00:09:14,387
we hold one hand up
as an all-clear signal.

229
00:09:14,454 --> 00:09:16,356
After that, we press the buttons together.

230
00:09:16,423 --> 00:09:18,792
When the control operator says,
"The train is ready to go,"

231
00:09:18,858 --> 00:09:20,860
we push the green button

232
00:09:20,927 --> 00:09:22,028
- with our hand up.
- "Go."

233
00:09:22,095 --> 00:09:23,296
- Go.
- Go.

234
00:09:23,363 --> 00:09:24,431
When you push the button,

235
00:09:24,497 --> 00:09:26,066
the train will leave the platform.

236
00:09:26,666 --> 00:09:29,302
While the train is running,
we need to wave and observe it

237
00:09:29,369 --> 00:09:30,970
to check the guests' safety

238
00:09:31,037 --> 00:09:32,572
with one hand on the station stopper.

239
00:09:32,906 --> 00:09:34,974
The moment you realize
the guests are in danger,

240
00:09:35,041 --> 00:09:36,276
you flick it

241
00:09:36,342 --> 00:09:38,878
- to stop the train.
- Just like that?

242
00:09:38,945 --> 00:09:42,015
- Let's send this train on its course.
- Okay.

243
00:09:42,082 --> 00:09:43,416
Should I take the other post?

244
00:09:43,483 --> 00:09:45,251
WONHEE GOES TO POST 1
Great idea.

245
00:09:45,318 --> 00:09:47,353
Please take on Post 6.

246
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:50,023
Once you confirm
that everyone is fastened securely,

247
00:09:50,090 --> 00:09:51,391
raise your hand...

248
00:09:52,092 --> 00:09:53,093
THROWS HER ARM UP

249
00:09:53,159 --> 00:09:54,661
...and push the yellow button.

250
00:09:55,462 --> 00:09:57,864
The sound just now means
the train is ready to go.

251
00:09:57,931 --> 00:09:59,199
It's the control operator's turn.

252
00:09:59,432 --> 00:10:02,168
The train is ready to go.

253
00:10:02,235 --> 00:10:03,203
Go!

254
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:04,671
THE GREEN BUTTONS HAVE BEEN PUSHED

255
