Wonhee of ILLIT

514
00:20:18,784 --> 00:20:20,953
and Eunchae of LE SSERAFIM.

515
00:20:21,353 --> 00:20:23,789
THANK YOU FOR THE WARM WELCOME
Let's say goodbye.

516
00:20:26,659 --> 00:20:30,663
WAVING UNTIL THE LAST SECOND

517
00:20:30,730 --> 00:20:32,531
<i>What did I just do?</i>

518
00:20:32,598 --> 00:20:33,933
SHIFT AT AMAZON EXPRESS ENDS

519
00:20:33,999 --> 00:20:34,834
<i>My mind went blank.</i>

520
00:20:35,568 --> 00:20:37,636
How was it for you?

521
00:20:37,703 --> 00:20:39,772
That was more intense than I imagined.

522
00:20:39,839 --> 00:20:43,209
I didn't expect to face such a big crowd.

523
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:46,011
I think I'll dream about this.

524
00:20:46,078 --> 00:20:49,715
- It was an invaluable experience.
- You can say that again.

525
00:20:49,782 --> 00:20:53,385
- It was so nerve-racking, too.
- Yeah.

526
00:20:53,452 --> 00:20:54,887
It was nice seeing all the teenagers...

527
00:20:54,954 --> 00:20:56,889
- Good job.
- Thank you for everything.

528
00:20:56,956 --> 00:20:57,957
Great work.

529
00:20:58,023 --> 00:20:59,925
MAJOR RESPECT
You're incredible.

530
00:20:59,992 --> 00:21:01,360
MAJOR RESPECT AGAIN
You are amazing.

531
00:21:01,427 --> 00:21:02,461
Thank you.

532
00:21:02,895 --> 00:21:04,497
Are you hungry?

533
00:21:04,563 --> 00:21:05,531
- Yes!
- Yes!

534
00:21:05,598 --> 00:21:07,933
Why don't we go to the cafeteria?

535
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:09,401
- Finally.
- Shall we?

536
00:21:09,468 --> 00:21:11,837
- Every bite is going to be worth it.
- Totally.

537
00:21:11,904 --> 00:21:13,939
Let's go.
I hear your cafeteria serves amazing food.

538
00:21:14,173 --> 00:21:15,541
Our cafeteria is incredible.

539
00:21:15,608 --> 00:21:17,243
- Let's get our lunch.
- Sounds great.

540
00:21:17,309 --> 00:21:18,878
- I'm ready.
- Yes.

541
00:21:22,715 --> 00:21:26,152
THIS IS THE FAMOUS STAFF CAFETERIA

542
00:21:27,253 --> 00:21:29,688
- Finally, it's lunch time.
- Yes, finally.

543
00:21:30,122 --> 00:21:31,457
What a nice setup.

544
00:21:31,524 --> 00:21:33,559
They offer three options today.

545
00:21:34,693 --> 00:21:35,995
Everything looks so good.

546
00:21:36,495 --> 00:21:37,763
- Can I take one?
- Yes.

547
00:21:37,830 --> 00:21:39,064
EXCITING MEALTIME

548
00:21:39,131 --> 00:21:41,934
I bet everything will taste incredible.

549
00:21:42,001 --> 00:21:44,703
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

550
00:21:44,770 --> 00:21:46,338
WONHEE IS ALSO PICKING UP FOOD

551
00:21:46,405 --> 00:21:47,907
We get dessert, too.

552
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:48,874
Right.

553
00:21:50,643 --> 00:21:52,077
This is solid.

554
00:21:52,144 --> 00:21:53,646
- Thank you.
- Enjoy.

555
00:21:53,712 --> 00:21:54,947
SO HAPPY AFTER THE SHIFT

556
00:21:57,850 --> 00:21:59,018
I can't wait to dig in.

557
00:21:59,084 --> 00:22:01,587
It's finally lunchtime.
You did a great job today.

558
00:22:01,654 --> 00:22:03,589
You too, Eunchae.

559
00:22:03,656 --> 00:22:05,057
INTROVERTS OUTDID THEMSELVES

560
00:22:05,124 --> 00:22:07,993
- We've earned this.
- Definitely.

561
00:22:08,060 --> 00:22:10,196
- Bon appétit.
- Bon appétit.

562
00:22:11,430 --> 00:22:13,432
FIRST, A BITE OF SIDE DISH

563
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:15,701
YUM

564
00:22:16,001 --> 00:22:17,236
GRINS

565
00:22:18,504 --> 00:22:21,907
WONHEE TAKES A BITE AFTER EUNCHAE

566
00:22:22,374 --> 00:22:24,343
This is the <i>jjamppong </i>soup.

567
00:22:26,545 --> 00:22:27,580
- Awesome.
- Oh, my.

568
00:22:27,646 --> 00:22:29,114
This looks so good.

569
00:22:29,348 --> 00:22:30,916
Thank you.

570
00:22:31,984 --> 00:22:33,152
So delicious.

571
00:22:33,219 --> 00:22:35,087
HAPPY MEAL WITH EXTRA SNACKS

572
00:22:40,626 --> 00:22:43,028
THIS IS IT

573
00:22:43,495 --> 00:22:45,231
This cafeteria is amazing.

574
00:22:45,297 --> 00:22:46,265
It's so good.

575
00:22:46,899 --> 00:22:48,767
It was a great experience.

576
00:22:48,834 --> 00:22:49,668
- Right?
- You know...

577
00:22:50,035 --> 00:22:52,071
The ride operators are incredible.

578
00:22:52,137 --> 00:22:55,407
I got so nervous
that I tensed up these muscles.

579
00:22:55,474 --> 00:22:58,711
- They got numb and started to shake.
- Mine too.

580
00:22:59,511 --> 00:23:01,947
How are you around strangers?

581
00:23:02,014 --> 00:23:05,384
Aren't you good with people?

582
00:23:05,584 --> 00:23:07,920
- I make an effort to relax.
- So it takes work?

583
00:23:08,120 --> 00:23:10,956
It's not easy to open up to people.

584
00:23:11,023 --> 00:23:15,694
My social skills improved
while working on <i>Eunchae's Star Diary</i>,

585
00:23:16,161 --> 00:23:19,298
but I've gotten worse
after the show ended.

586
00:23:19,365 --> 00:23:21,000
How long does it take
for you to make friends?

587
00:23:21,166 --> 00:23:23,636
Personally, my standards are high.

588
00:23:23,869 --> 00:23:27,740
I don't use the word "friend" lightly.

589
00:23:27,806 --> 00:23:29,775
I'm like you on that point.

590
00:23:37,116 --> 00:23:39,184
- Do you have any hobbies?
- Hobbies?

591
00:23:39,251 --> 00:23:40,386
I do, actually.

592
00:23:41,120 --> 00:23:43,155
The weather has gotten warmer,

593
00:23:43,389 --> 00:23:46,258
so I've been enjoying
long walks by myself.

594
00:23:46,325 --> 00:23:49,495
After dinner, I'd go out on my own

595
00:23:49,561 --> 00:23:51,397
and take a stroll across Yongsan.

596
00:23:52,197 --> 00:23:55,834
Sometimes after work,
I walk to the dorm on my own.

597
00:23:55,901 --> 00:23:58,637
Back when I was really into walking,

598
00:23:58,704 --> 00:24:00,639
- I used to walk to work.
- I do that, too.

599
00:24:00,706 --> 00:24:01,807
Do you have hobbies?

600
00:24:01,874 --> 00:24:02,875
I have a few.

601
00:24:02,942 --> 00:24:04,476
I don't dig into one thing.

602
00:24:04,543 --> 00:24:06,312
- You try bits of everything?
- That's right.

603
00:24:06,378 --> 00:24:07,513
- Tell me more.
- Still,

604
00:24:07,579 --> 00:24:09,548
I read books...

605
00:24:09,615 --> 00:24:11,417
But it's so cringe to say that out loud.

606
00:24:11,483 --> 00:24:12,451
How come?

607
00:24:12,518 --> 00:24:13,619
It gives me the ick.

608
00:24:13,686 --> 00:24:15,554
I don't want to sound pretentious.

609
00:24:15,621 --> 00:24:18,657
Anyway, I lend books to people around me,
including my staff.

610
00:24:19,091 --> 00:24:20,426
- So--
- Really? Lend me some.

611
00:24:20,492 --> 00:24:22,127
- Of course, hit me up anytime.
- Are you sure?

612
00:24:22,194 --> 00:24:23,829
What's your favorite so far?

613
00:24:23,896 --> 00:24:25,631
I love thrillers.

614
00:24:25,698 --> 00:24:26,832
I like thrillers, too.

615
00:24:26,899 --> 00:24:28,434
I enjoyed <i>Hunter With a Scalpel</i>.

616
00:24:29,268 --> 00:24:30,169
The title sucks you in.

617
00:24:30,235 --> 00:24:31,837
- Sounds interesting.
- It's fascinating.

618
00:24:31,904 --> 00:24:33,305
Have you gone to late-night screenings?

619
00:24:33,372 --> 00:24:36,942
Adults can see late-night screenings
to horror movies.

620
00:24:37,009 --> 00:24:40,045
I've gone to those,
but not for a horror movie.

621
00:24:40,980 --> 00:24:42,848
I'm a big horror fan, though.

622
00:24:43,148 --> 00:24:45,084
- My group members are also fans.
- The problem is,

623
00:24:45,150 --> 00:24:46,585
my group members are not.

624
00:24:46,652 --> 00:24:47,820
Come join us.

625
00:24:47,886 --> 00:24:48,921
WATCH HORROR MOVIES WITH US

626
00:24:48,988 --> 00:24:51,423
One time, I really wanted to watch
this one horror movie,

627
00:24:51,490 --> 00:24:54,093
so I dragged everyone with me after work.

628
00:24:54,393 --> 00:24:57,529
They don't like horror in general,
but they still came along.

629
00:24:57,596 --> 00:24:58,564
But after the screening...

630
00:24:58,630 --> 00:25:01,400
I guess it was scarier
than they had expected,

631
00:25:01,467 --> 00:25:03,369
so they complained to me afterward.

632
00:25:04,169 --> 00:25:05,871
I have that memory.

633
00:25:05,938 --> 00:25:08,040
I love the genre.
I get scared, but I enjoy it.

634
00:25:08,107 --> 00:25:09,441
- Same.
- Really?

635
00:25:09,508 --> 00:25:10,943
I can't stay cool

636
00:25:11,010 --> 00:25:13,779
- Want to catch one at night together?
- or stay unfazed...

637
00:25:13,846 --> 00:25:14,980
I'd love to.

638
00:25:15,280 --> 00:25:16,782
Really? That's a promise.

639
00:25:16,849 --> 00:25:20,486
- Nobody would join me.
- All my members love horror,

640
00:25:20,552 --> 00:25:21,720
- Seriously?
- except for Yunah.

641
00:25:21,787 --> 00:25:22,855
That's great.

642
00:25:22,921 --> 00:25:24,823
Nice, I'll join you guys one day.

643
00:25:24,890 --> 00:25:26,091
PLEASE JOIN US
Awesome.

644
00:25:26,158 --> 00:25:27,960
What was your life like at 20?

645
00:25:28,027 --> 00:25:31,330
Weren't you at <i>Kōhaku Uta Gassen</i>
on New Year's Eve?

646
00:25:31,397 --> 00:25:32,231
JAPANESE SHOW

647
00:25:32,798 --> 00:25:33,832
- Yes.
- Me too.

648
00:25:33,899 --> 00:25:35,701
But I wasn't legal in Japan.

649
00:25:35,768 --> 00:25:36,602
I KNOW WHAT YOU MEAN

650
00:25:36,668 --> 00:25:38,871
I couldn't really enjoy it
while I was there.

651
00:25:38,937 --> 00:25:41,407
I didn't get to celebrate as much
on New Year's Day.

652
00:25:41,840 --> 00:25:43,542
- I was the same way.
- Right?

653
00:25:43,609 --> 00:25:45,611
When I came back to Korea the next day,

654
00:25:45,677 --> 00:25:47,579
- I had a drink with my parents.
- I did that, too.

655
00:25:48,113 --> 00:25:53,152
I tried alcohol over a family dinner.

656
00:25:53,519 --> 00:25:55,687
Still, those little things
made all the difference.

657
00:25:55,754 --> 00:25:59,258
When my group debuted,
I was the only minor on the team.

658
00:25:59,792 --> 00:26:02,761
Whenever we had a team dinner
or went out to eat together,

659
00:26:02,828 --> 00:26:06,265
I was the only one
who couldn't order drinks.

660
00:26:06,331 --> 00:26:07,800
So after becoming legal,

661
00:26:08,200 --> 00:26:11,403
I was happy to be able to enjoy
our time together more.

662
00:26:11,637 --> 00:26:13,338
It's pretty much the same with me,

663
00:26:13,405 --> 00:26:15,607
but Iroha's still a minor.

664
00:26:16,108 --> 00:26:17,609
She's feeling left out.

665
00:26:18,077 --> 00:26:19,311
How cute.

666
00:26:20,779 --> 00:26:22,915
But she'll be legal next year, right?

667
00:26:22,981 --> 00:26:25,084
CONGRATS
So everyone in ILLIT will be legal?

668
00:26:25,150 --> 00:26:26,051
That's just...

669
00:26:26,118 --> 00:26:30,022
It rings so strange to me.

670
00:26:30,089 --> 00:26:34,259
You're the youngest member of LE SSERAFIM.

671
00:26:34,660 --> 00:26:37,463
If you could choose,
where would you fall in the age order?

672
00:26:37,529 --> 00:26:39,498
I've always loved being the youngest,

673
00:26:39,565 --> 00:26:42,201
but I've changed my mind recently.

674
00:26:42,267 --> 00:26:44,703
Almost everyone
in new idol groups these days

675
00:26:44,770 --> 00:26:48,407
is younger than me.

676
00:26:48,474 --> 00:26:51,076
While looking at them, I've come to think

677
00:26:52,311 --> 00:26:55,080
that it might be nice to have
one member younger than me,

678
00:26:55,147 --> 00:26:56,582
just like you do.

679
00:26:56,648 --> 00:26:58,484
I just want one younger member.

680
00:26:58,984 --> 00:27:00,419
- So fourth, I suppose.
- Fourth?

681
00:27:00,486 --> 00:27:02,121
I'd like that.

682
00:27:02,187 --> 00:27:04,957
Who would you choose if you could make
one member younger than you?

683
00:27:05,023 --> 00:27:07,392
Kazuha, all the way.

684
00:27:07,459 --> 00:27:08,760
Kazuha.

685
00:27:09,361 --> 00:27:13,098
3 YEARS APART
Kazuha and I are closest in age,

686
00:27:13,165 --> 00:27:15,067
so we're really close.

687
00:27:15,134 --> 00:27:19,371
When I monitor my group's web content,
I look most relaxed when I'm with her.

688
00:27:19,438 --> 00:27:22,975
I think we could have a fun dynamic
if we swapped our ages.

689
00:27:23,041 --> 00:27:26,745
I honestly can't picture other members
being younger than me.

690
00:27:29,348 --> 00:27:30,616
What about you, Wonhee?

691
00:27:30,682 --> 00:27:32,751
Three members were born in the same year.

692
00:27:32,818 --> 00:27:33,752
MINJU, YUNAH, MOKA

693
00:27:33,819 --> 00:27:36,188
The three of them are very tight.

694
00:27:36,255 --> 00:27:37,923
- Because they're the same age?
- Yes.

695
00:27:37,990 --> 00:27:41,627
I wonder what it would be like
to be the same age as them.

696
00:27:41,960 --> 00:27:42,794
CHUCKLES

697
00:27:42,861 --> 00:27:43,829
Same age as them?

698
00:27:45,097 --> 00:27:47,065
What changed for you at 20?

699
00:27:47,132 --> 00:27:49,334
Did you have to take on
more responsibilities?

700
00:27:49,768 --> 00:27:55,274
I don't have as many people
reminding me about things anymore.

701
00:27:55,340 --> 00:27:57,843
It felt like I had to manage
everything on my own.

702
00:27:58,010 --> 00:28:01,680
- I just wanted to do well.
- Right, I get what you mean.

703
00:28:01,747 --> 00:28:02,915
AGE 20 COMES WITH RESPONSIBILITIES

704
00:28:03,148 --> 00:28:05,184
SNACK TIME IS A MUST

705
00:28:06,018 --> 00:28:08,453
CRUNCH

706
00:28:08,787 --> 00:28:10,455
A churro at Everland.

707
00:28:11,290 --> 00:28:13,091
An Ever-churro.

708
00:28:13,158 --> 00:28:16,261
WRAPPING UP THE DAY WITH SWEET SNACKS

709
00:28:16,328 --> 00:28:19,198
How was your Everland experience with me?

710
00:28:19,565 --> 00:28:21,867
Basically, I was new to everything.

711
00:28:21,934 --> 00:28:23,802
But with you by my side,

712
00:28:23,869 --> 00:28:26,638
every moment became
an unforgettable memory.

713
00:28:26,705 --> 00:28:27,806
- Really?
- It was therapeutic.

714
00:28:27,873 --> 00:28:29,107
<i>I got to be outdoors</i>

715
00:28:29,174 --> 00:28:30,342
<i>and meet so many people,</i>

716
00:28:30,409 --> 00:28:32,244
<i>especially the cheerful teenagers.</i>

717
00:28:32,311 --> 00:28:35,447
LAUGHTER NEVER STOPPED

718
00:28:35,514 --> 00:28:37,849
<i>- We even danced.</i>
<i>- It was therapeutic.</i>

719
00:28:37,916 --> 00:28:39,685
TODAY FELT LIKE A NICE BREAK
<i>Really? I'm so glad.</i>

720
00:28:41,887 --> 00:28:44,790
You got on the roller coaster
to celebrate my turning 20.

721
00:28:44,856 --> 00:28:46,391
Could you give me advice as well?

722
00:28:47,192 --> 00:28:49,761
I still can't believe you're 20 this year.

723
00:28:49,828 --> 00:28:53,765
It's crazy.
How can this little cutie be an adult?

724
00:28:53,999 --> 00:28:57,135
- You look 17 at most.
- "This little cutie"?

725
00:28:58,103 --> 00:28:59,838
You're 20? My gosh.

726
00:29:00,038 --> 00:29:02,007
FROM 21-YEAR-OLD TO 20-YEAR-OLD
Here's my advice.

727
00:29:03,108 --> 00:29:04,076
My gosh.

728
00:29:04,142 --> 00:29:05,744
About turning 20.

729
00:29:06,478 --> 00:29:09,481
I'd been looking forward to it as well.

730
00:29:09,548 --> 00:29:11,250
I couldn't wait to hit 20.

731
00:29:11,316 --> 00:29:13,252
I even wondered,
"Why am I the only minor?"

732
00:29:13,318 --> 00:29:15,053
I was that impatient.

733
00:29:15,120 --> 00:29:17,356
But when I finally reached that age,

734
00:29:17,422 --> 00:29:19,558
I developed a new sense of responsibility.

735
00:29:19,625 --> 00:29:20,959
Nobody gave me the push,

736
00:29:21,026 --> 00:29:22,661
but I felt that way on my own.

737
00:29:22,961 --> 00:29:26,665
You might also develop it
and feel burdened by it.

738
00:29:26,732 --> 00:29:29,601
If you do, shake it off
and be your usual self.

739
00:29:29,935 --> 00:29:32,571
I hope you stay as cheerful as ever.

740
00:29:32,638 --> 00:29:33,872
Thank you.

741
00:29:34,139 --> 00:29:35,073
Congrats.

742
00:29:35,140 --> 00:29:36,608
- Thank you.
- I can't believe it.

743
00:29:36,675 --> 00:29:38,577
- I'll be cheering for you.
- Thank you.

744
00:29:38,644 --> 00:29:40,646
- Thank you for coming.
- Hope all your dreams come true.

745
00:29:40,712 --> 00:29:42,214
- I will.
- Go for them.

746
00:29:42,281 --> 00:29:43,348
I will!

747
00:29:44,182 --> 00:29:46,184
- Thank you so much.
- Great work today.

748
00:29:46,251 --> 00:29:47,419
Thank you.

749
00:29:47,486 --> 00:29:48,687
"I HOPE YOU STAY CHEERFUL...

750
00:29:48,754 --> 00:29:50,088
Take care.

751
00:29:50,155 --> 00:29:51,757
...EVEN WITH NEW RESPONSIBILITIES"

752
00:29:52,124 --> 00:29:54,192
A NEW CHALLENGE FOR A HEALTHIER LIFE

753
00:29:54,893 --> 00:29:57,763
BOXING
<i>This feels easy. Maybe I have a talent.</i>

754
00:29:58,330 --> 00:30:00,232
TRAINING PARTNER
<i>This is pretty cool.</i>

755
00:30:00,299 --> 00:30:02,734
EPISODE 5 GIRLIE
PATRICIA

756
00:30:03,869 --> 00:30:05,304
<i>It's not so bad so far.</i>

757
00:30:06,538 --> 00:30:08,974
THE GIRLIES TAKE ON BOXING
You're something else.

758
00:30:09,574 --> 00:30:11,576
CHAMPIONS FROM AFAR

759
00:30:11,643 --> 00:30:12,878
Hang on!

760
00:30:12,944 --> 00:30:15,347
COMPLETE DISASTER UP CLOSE
What on earth?

761
00:30:16,014 --> 00:30:18,050
HELLISH BOOT CAMP BEGINS
Coach, please!

762
00:30:18,283 --> 00:30:19,284
This is just...

763
00:30:19,351 --> 00:30:20,619
- Is it that bad?
- It's terrible.

764
00:30:20,686 --> 00:30:22,521
- Just one more set?
